This cluster represents a cross-cultural semantic space where diverse metaphysical systems—from Zande witchcraft to Vedantic idealism—converge on the theme of explaining causality through intentional, anthropomorphized, or transcendent agents. The vectors share a high coherence (0.78) around the idea that human perception imposes agency onto natural phenomena, whether as witchcraft, cosmic forces, or spiritual intelligence, to bridge gaps in empirical causality.

**Conclusion:** The semantic concept of this cluster is **Supernatural Causality and Anthropomorphic Agency**.

